From: CompSciOrBust <54033033+CompSciOrBust@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ldr: honour DisableProgramVerification on 23.0.0 and later

Before 23.0.0, pm read the DisableProgramVerification configuration
item from spl and told the loader to stop requiring a valid ACID
signature.  23.0.0 removed spl from pm, so on later firmware nothing
acts on the item and every program must be signed with Nintendo's key.
This OS has no such signatures.  Read the item in the loader at
start-up instead.  As before, it only takes effect on a development
unit.

---
diff --git a/stratosphere/loader/source/ldr_main.cpp b/stratosphere/loader/source/ldr_main.cpp
index 5e4d8ca06..709141e4f 100644
--- a/stratosphere/loader/source/ldr_main.cpp
+++ b/stratosphere/loader/source/ldr_main.cpp
@@ -140,6 +140,12 @@ namespace ams {
         ldr::SetDevelopmentForAntiDowngradeCheck(spl::IsDevelopment());
         ldr::SetDevelopmentForAcidSignatureCheck(spl::IsDevelopment());
 
+        /* Honour the configuration item that disables program verification. Before 23.0.0, pm */
+        /* read it and told us; pm no longer uses spl, so nothing would otherwise act on it. */
+        if (spl::IsDisabledProgramVerification()) {
+            ldr::SetEnabledProgramVerification(false);
+        }
+
         /* Register the loader services. */
         ldr::RegisterServiceSessions();
 
